          "bbox": [
            0.526,
            0.026,
            0.842,
            0.043
          ],
          "content": "Chapter 11 — Keeping Time with the Skies"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.868,
            0.008,
            0.944,
            0.081
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_7_image_1.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.083,
            0.35,
            0.399
          ],
          "content": "In Activity 11.1, we also observed that the position of the Moon at sunrise (or sunset) appeared to be shifted on successive days. This happens because, as shown in Fig. 11.6, the Moon moves ahead in its orbit while the Earth completes one rotation about its axis in 24 hours. Earth needs to rotate some more for the Moon to appear in nearly the same spot in the sky."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.357,
            0.082,
            0.564,
            0.147
          ],
          "content": "(b) In the same time of one day, the Moon would revolve a bit further in its orbit around the Earth."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.357,
            0.081,
            0.888,
            0.201
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [
            {
              "bbox": [
                0.37,
                0.208,
                0.575,
                0.287
              ],
              "content": "(c) So I will find the Moon overhead about 50 minutes later than today, when the Earth has rotated some more."
            }
          ],
          "image_source": "images/page_7_image_4.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.559,
            0.204,
            0.749,
            0.36
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [
            {
              "bbox": [
                0.75,
                0.203,
                0.931,
                0.285
              ],
              "content": "(a) Today the Moon is overhead. The Earth will rotate once in one day, and I will be back at this same position."
            },
            {
              "bbox": [
                0.404,
                0.365,
                0.826,
                0.4
              ],
              "content": "Fig. 11.6: The Moon takes about 50 minutes longer to come back to nearly the same position in the sky."
            }
          ],
          "image_source": "images/page_7_image_6.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.132,
            0.409,
            0.301,
            0.432
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "A step further"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.135,
            0.443,
            0.767,
            0.562
          ],
          "content": "The Moon phases do not happen due to Earth’s shadow. It is an incorrect explanation for the Moon’s phases that Earth’s shadow falls on it. As we have learnt, the phases of the Moon occur due to the relative change in orientation of the Sun, Moon, and Earth as the Moon revolves around the Earth. The Earth’s shadow on the Moon causes a lunar eclipse, not the Moon’s phases as we learnt earlier (in chapter ‘Earth, Moon and the Sun’ in the Curiosity, Grade 7)."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.136,
            0.562,
            0.767,
            0.63
          ],
          "content": "Lunar eclipses can only happen on a full Moon day and solar eclipses can happen only on a new Moon day. But they do not occur every month because of the small tilt of the Moon’s orbit with respect to the Earth’s orbit around the Sun. Position"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.128,
            0.622,
            0.771,
            0.893
          ],
          "content": "",
